.TH CJSON_LIST_PUSH 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cjson_list_push \- append a child to an array node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cjson.h>

ccol_retval_t cjson_list_push(cjson arr, cjson child);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Appends child to the end of arr.  Ownership of child transfers to arr
unconditionally: on success the array owns child; on failure child is
deep-freed by cjson_list_push.  Do not free child after calling this
function regardless of the return value.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success, ccol_invalid_args, or ccol_not_enough_memory.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cjson_list_get (3),
.BR cjson_create_list (3)
